<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The feral insect faction keeps its raids, its infestations, cave and ancient
		danger spawns, deep drilling and the thumper bosses - but loses its bases on
		the world map.

		Why: with the two insector tribes in the world there were three insect
		factions on the overworld, two of them hostile and holding settlements,
		which read as redundant. Ruling 2026-09-20.

		VFEI2 turns the vanilla hidden insect faction into a settling faction by
		adding <settlementGenerationWeight>1</settlementGenerationWeight> to it
		(1.6/Patches/InsectFactionPatch.xml, a PatchOperationAdd). This patch puts
		the weight back to 0, so world generation places no hive towns. Our mod
		loads after VFEI2, so this replace runs after their add and wins.

		Everything this switches off is keyed on "is this settlement owned by
		Faction.OfInsects": the infested territory and its world-map overlay, the
		insect map generation on those tiles (creep, 20-30 wild hives, and the
		geneline boss that only spawns on a map owned by that faction), and the
		distance-based infestation MTB. Raids and infestations are unaffected: they
		come from the faction, not from its settlements.

		Still reachable afterwards: the geneline bosses through the thumper
		buildings, and the Emerging Hive quest, which can still turn its site into a
		real hive settlement and so create one infested region. That one is treated
		as a feature, not a hole.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/FactionDef[defName="Insect"]/settlementGenerationWeight</xpath>
		<value>
			<settlementGenerationWeight>0</settlementGenerationWeight>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
